{
  "component": "Slider Field",
  "description": "A form field that pairs a range slider with a label, a numeric output value and helper text. Four state variants cover Default, Hover, Focus and Disabled, and the label and description can each be switched off. PURPOSE: Lets a user pick a value along a continuous track, with the current value shown next to the label and guidance shown below the track. BEHAVIOUR: The Hover variant responds to pointer-over on the track or handle. The Focus variant adds a focus ring using Stroke/Focus Ring and Border/Focus/Default, which is what keyboard users see when the handle is tabbed to. The Disabled variant swaps the track and handle to Background/Disabled/Default and Border/Disabled/default and should block pointer and keyboard input. The filled portion of the track uses Background/Brand/Default and the remaining track uses Background/Brand/Secondary. COMPOSITION: No nested component instances were detected. Every part is a local frame: a Label frame holding the label text and a Slider Output frame, a Slider frame holding the Block (track and handle), and a Description text layer. If the code base already has a slider primitive, a form label or a helper text component, AI code generators should reuse those rather than rebuild them here. USAGE: Use when the value is approximate and the range matters more than precision, for example volume, opacity or a price filter. Use a number input when an exact figure is required, and a segmented control or radio group when the choices are discrete and few. The Slider Output should stay visible when the user needs to read back the exact number. CODE GENERATION NOTES: Render as input type=range or a div with role=slider carrying aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax, aria-valuenow and aria-valuetext. Tie the label to the control with a for or aria-labelledby reference, and the description with aria-describedby. Support Arrow keys for single steps, Page Up and Page Down for larger jumps, and Home and End for the bounds. State variants are visual only and should be driven by :hover, :focus-visible and the disabled attribute, not by separate components. Label and Description text are editable properties, so expose them as props rather than hard-coded strings.",
